{"page": 18, "text": "Net cash provided by (used in) financing activities 1,467 40 (252) (1,357) 712 (857)\nIn the third quarter of 2026, we continued to prudently invest in our lending products, including growing Cash App Borrow and Afterpay Post-Purchase given the strong unit economics and returns we have seen. Within our non-GAAP cash flow, we have deployed $1.4 billion in capital to grow our lending products over the last 12 months.29 We ended the quarter with $10.1 billion of total liquidity, with $9.2 billion in cash, cash equivalents, restricted cash, and investments in marketable debt securities, and $900 million available to be withdrawn from our revolving credit facility. Additionally, we had $809 million available to be withdrawn under our warehouse funding facilities. 28 Quarterly figures presented may not sum precisely due to rounding. 29 Capital deployed to grow lending products is calculated as the trailing twelve month change in our lending product balances (which consists of consumer receivables, net; loans held for sale; and loans held for investment, net), less the net financing provided by our warehouse facilities (i.e. proceeds net of repayments) over the same period. 15\nEarnings Webcast\nBlock (NYSE:XYZ) will host a conference call and earnings webcast at 2:00 p.m. Pacific time/5:00 p.m. Eastern time, November 3, 2026, to discuss these financial results. To register to participate in the conference call, or to listen to the live audio webcast, please visit the Events & Presentations section of Block\u2019s Investor Relations website at investors.block.xyz. A replay will be available on the same website following the call. We will release financial results for the fourth quarter of 2026 on February 24, 2027, after the market closes, and will also host a conference call and earnings webcast at 2:00 p.m. Pacific time/5:00 p.m. Eastern time on the same day to discuss those financial results.\nMedia Contact press@block.xyz Investor Relations Contact ir@block.xyz\nJack Dorsey Amrita Ahuja\n16\n"}
